<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moravian Compromise</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moravian Compromise was a set of laws adopted in 1905 that reorganised the Moravian Diet and its electoral system along national lines. Voters were enrolled in separate Czech and German registers, each electing a fixed share of the seats, and school administration was divided in the same way. It eased Czech–German conflict in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> and was later cited as a model of national autonomy within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg Monarchy</a>.</p></div>
